IOP disc image search and printf: sceCdSearchFile walks the mounted image's ISO9660 directories, and IOP printf
formats its arguments. Why: with only a disc image (CdImage) given, the IOP cdvdman searched just the virtual ISO
built from an extracted folder (CdRoot), which is not there, so every search failed. Jackass's FMODS.IRX opens its
FSB sound banks by device-less path (\DATA\PS2\SOUNDS\MISC\MENUFX.FSB;1) and logged "FMODFile_Open : ERROR - %s"
for each. printf printed that raw format; it now fills in a1-a3 and stack arguments. The virtual ISO is still
used when the image has no match. Test: ps2xIOP/tests/iop_import_tests.cpp testCdvdSearchFileImage.
Origin: this project (jackass-ps2-recomp), 2026-10-27.

